<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8863de290646> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Japan’s Henn na Hotel, which first opened in 2015 with a staff of robots, has cut its robotic workforce after the experience failed to reduce costs or workload for its employees." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8d97f2c0998c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "That’s when problems started to pile up, said the hotel’s general manager, Takeyoshi Oe." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/912038162472> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1913] 2 velociraptor robots positioned at check-in were also decommissioned because human workers essentially had to do their jobs for them and photocopy guests’ passports manually. [1913] 2 robot luggage carriers could only reach about 24 of the over 100 rooms in the hotel and failed in rain or snow. [1913] The hotel’s main concierge robot also didn’t know how to answer questions about flight schedules and nearby tourist attractions." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1913" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/962c9eb70c03> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Siri, Google Assistant, and Alexa can answer questions about local businesses’ opening and closing times, but Churi couldn’t." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1913" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b7b30c388e49> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "There were also humanoid concierge robots, but like Churi, they were also removed for being unable to answer basic tourist questions." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1867" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bc665793470d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Robots Ruin Robot Hotel" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1867" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c057e5d2a64e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Japan’s Henn na Hotel, which first opened in 2015 with a staff of robots, has cut its robotic workforce after the experience failed to reduce costs or workload for its employees." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c4c2a32270b0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "a delivery robot called Segway-Ninebot Loomo Delivery can zip goods around a building complex." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ccc719a569dd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "1 of the layoffs included a doll-shaped assistant in each hotel room called Churi." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1913" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/db2ec4ba0cf4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Japan’s robot hotel lays off half the robots after they created more work for humans" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1913" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dcd702b91210> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1914] Japan’s Henn na Hotel, which first opened in 2015 with a staff of robots, has cut its robotic workforce after the experience failed to reduce costs or workload for its employees." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/de1ebd8870f9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "1 guest complained that he was woken up regularly through the night by Churi, a virtual assistant robot that was put in each guest’s room." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1867" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e146627403de> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Toshifumi Nakamura, a former hotel guest, recalled that about half the puppy-size lobby dancers appeared to be broken or in need of charging when he visited in mid-2016." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1915" .

