<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0ade0075fb0f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Chinese e-commerce company Alibaba launched the Space Egg robot hotel porter late last year," ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0f6097bd35d5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "the Hilton in McLean, Va., employs a robot concierge." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2cfc2a1d97fa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "2 velociraptor robots positioned at check-in were also decommissioned because human workers essentially had to do their jobs for them and photocopy guests’ passports manually." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1913" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/359df3817be1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Hotels in the Yotel and Aloft chains in the U.S. use 3-feet high droids that deliver mail, toiletries and drinks to rooms." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/389b23ab23e2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The hotel’s main concierge robot also didn’t know how to answer questions about flight schedules and nearby tourist attractions." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1913" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/95bb53e90754> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "a Lenovo Smart Clock with a built-in Google assistant can turn the lights on or read you a bedtime story" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fddf2eac6307> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "2 robot luggage carriers could only reach about 24 of the over 100 rooms in the hotel and failed in rain or snow." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1913" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1c80d9775cdc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Atsushi Nishiguchi, a guest at the hotel in 2017, said that after an irate exchange with Churi he decided to phone the hotel reception, only to find there was no phone in the room because the assistant was intended to handle guests’ requests." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3106db76047b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“She got a bad reputation,” said Hideo Sawada, president of the travel company that owns the hotel." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/81d41415dc3f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“They were really slow and noisy, and would get stuck trying to go past each other,” said Taishi Mito, a guest at the hotel in 2017." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1915" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/860fd3827acf> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The hotel’s parent company, H.I.S., announced plans to construct eight more humanoid robot-staffed Henn na Hotels." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1914" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ab69c36c4278> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Hotel owner Hideo Sawada said he wanted to run “the most efficient hotel in the world” by staffing it almost exclusively with robots." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1867" .

